<title>FRANCE: SOCCER-BRAZIL 1 ENGLAND 0 - TOURNOI DE FRANCE RESULT.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZIL 1 ENGLAND 0 - TOURNOI DE FRANCE RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil beat England 1-0 (halftime</p>
<p>0-0) in their Tournoi de France soccer match on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scorer: Romario 61</p>
<p>Attendance: 33,000</p>
<p>England -- 1-David Seaman; 15-Martin Keown (2-Gary Neville</p>
<p>21), 5-Gareth Southgate, 12-Sol Campbell; 14-Philip Neville,</p>
<p>8-Paul Gascoigne, 19-Paul Scholes (11-Robert Lee 75), 4-Paul</p>
<p>Ince, 6-Graeme Le Saux; 10-Teddy Sheringham (20-Ian Wright 75),</p>
<p>9-Alan Shearer.</p>
<p>Brazil -- 1-Taffarel; 2-Cafu, 15-Celio Silva, 3-Aldair,</p>
<p>6-Roberto Carlos; 19-Flavio Conceicao, 8-Dunga, 20-Denilson</p>
<p>(13-Djalminha 22), 10-Leonardo (17-Ze Roberto 82); 11-Romario,</p>
<p>9-Ronaldo.</p>
<p>Referee: John Jairo Toro Rendon (Colombia)</p>
<p>    Standings   P   W   D   L   F   A    Pts</p>
<p> England	  3   2   0   1   3   1     6</p>
<p> Brazil	   3   1   2   0   5   4     5</p>
<p> France	   2   0   1   1   1   2     1</p>
<p> Italy	    2   0   1   1   3   5     1</p>
<p>Remaining match: June 11 - France v Italy, in Paris</p>
</text>
